cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this data, please cite it — and cite the source papers for any finding that matters to your work."
type: dataset
title: "POTS / Dysautonomia Cross-Condition Literature Findings"
version: "v1.2"
date-released: "2026-10-22"
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/erinmagennis/pots-findings"
authors:
  - family-names: "Magennis"
    given-names: "Erin"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-9013-8052"
abstract: >-
  148,186 structured findings machine-extracted from 11,519 papers across the POTS,
  dysautonomia and comorbid-condition literature (ME/CFS, Ehlers-Danlos and hypermobility,
  MCAS, fibromyalgia, IBS, small-fiber neuropathy, long COVID, autism, migraine, Sjogren's,
  PANS/PANDAS). Distributed as five self-contained packages sharing zero papers. Every
  finding carries the verbatim source span it was drawn from plus its source paper's PMID
  and DOI, and explicit provenance for every ontology identifier. Scientific fidelity is
  unmeasured: all quality checks verify well-formedness, not correct interpretation of
  sources. Not medical advice.
keywords:
  - "POTS"
  - "postural orthostatic tachycardia syndrome"
  - "dysautonomia"
  - "ME/CFS"
  - "Ehlers-Danlos syndrome"
  - "hypermobility"
  - "fibromyalgia"
  - "mast cell activation syndrome"
  - "long COVID"
  - "small fiber neuropathy"
  - "autism"
  - "migraine"
  - "literature extraction"
  - "text and data mining"
  - "biomarkers"
